mhvtl-control for Debian
=================

mhvtl-control is installed but neither enabled nor started. To run it:

  systemctl enable --now mhvtl-control

It listens on http://127.0.0.1:8080 by default. Options, including the
listen address, an API token and TLS, are set in
/etc/mhvtl-control/mhvtl-control.env (mode 0600); restart mhvtl-control after
changing it. mhvtl-control refuses to bind a non-loopback address without a
token.

mhvtl-control finds mhVTL's libraries in /etc/mhvtl/device.conf and talks to the
running mhVTL daemons, so it is useful once the mhvtl package is set up.
It tolerates mhVTL starting after it, and mhVTL restarts.

The configuration editor is read-only until you turn writes on. That needs
an API token, TLS on a non-loopback listen address, and the configuration
helper's units:

  systemctl enable --now mhvtl-control-apply.socket
  systemctl enable mhvtl-control-apply-recover.service

mhvtl-control(8) and
https://github.com/ciroiriarte/mhvtl-control#configuration-editor explain
what an apply does to running libraries and how to turn writes off again.
